<title>INDIA: Indian soybean steady on limited arrivals, demand.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean steady on limited arrivals, demand.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were steady in the markets of central India and plant delivery condition on Monday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Arrivals were limited and purchasing demand from processing plants was also limited. Business volume was dull and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were slightly down in very limited trading. The undertone was easy.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were almost steady in dull trading as buyers and sellers were both limited. Soymeal yellow was $304-305 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) in bulk for export. Rapeseed extraction was $118 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) for export and was 4,050 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition. Business was dull and the undertone was steady.</p>
